## Consumer module entrance

The trial release owner selects the two public compiler front-door names when
creating the reviewed build-values file. They are CSE presentation names; they
are not inferred from the login shell's default compiler or `PrgEnv-*` module.
This workspace records:

- shared compiler front door: `cse/{{ values.shared.compiler.public_name }}`
- platform compiler front door: `cse/{{ values.platform.compiler.public_name }}`

After the release's module root is published on the site `MODULEPATH`, enter one
surface and exactly one payload lane:

```bash
module load cse/{{ values.shared.compiler.public_name }}  # or cse/{{ values.platform.compiler.public_name }}
module load Serial                                        # or MPI
module load <package>/<version>
```

The `init-` prefix used by the current trial selections is trial-only. The full
Stack Composer renderer's canonical convention is `cse/<Compiler>`, followed
by the same short lane selector. The generated front door owns the reviewed
compiler-module sequence and the selected surface's Foundation, Core, Common,
and lane-module paths. A CSE-built MPI lane loads its exact generated provider
module. A platform Cray MPI lane requires the reviewed Cray MPI module to
already be active and does not replace the site programming environment. In
both cases the lane then exposes only its package-module root. The generated
modules record the resolved commands in `CSE_CC`, `CSE_CXX`, `CSE_FC`,
`CSE_MPICC`, `CSE_MPICXX`, and `CSE_MPIFC`.

For a CSE-built GCC surface backed by external Cray MPICH, the completed locked
package builds establish the selected headers, link inputs, and runtime closure
for the Spack build plane. The workspace `MPI` selector exposes the selected
Cray MPICH simple wrappers for ordinary validation. It binds `mpicc`, `mpicxx`,
`mpifort`, `mpif90`, and `mpif77` to the compiler already activated by the CSE
front door through the `MPICH_*` compiler overrides. It prepends the recorded
runtime paths without loading a compiler-selecting `PrgEnv-*`, loading the
platform Cray MPICH module chain, or replacing `CC`, `CXX`, or `FC`.

The external-MPI consumer record is presentation metadata only. It is derived
from the selected static-catalog scope and is not used by an environment spec,
package roster, package overlay, or Spack toolchain constraint. The exact
prefix, simple-wrapper paths, and allowlisted runtime paths are recorded in
`presentation/mpi-consumer-candidates.yaml`. Launcher selection remains a
separate live site fact and is not inferred from the compile-wrapper prefix.

After all package installs and package-module refreshes finish, copy the
independent presentation layer into the module root recorded by the current
values with:

```bash
./cse-build login publish-modules
```

For restricted trial values, this is a restricted CSE team-review checkpoint,
not public promotion. It does not publish the static catalog, create a
publication workspace, change filesystem audience, or refresh or replace a
package module tree. It copies only `cse/<public-name>` and
`<compiler>/lanes/{Serial,MPI}` files. A CSE-built-compiler/external-MPI
selector whose status is
`multi-node-validation-required` remains usable from the workspace
`modulefiles/` tree but is withheld from the release module root. Publish it
only after a native multi-node launch succeeds through the site's approved
Slurm or Cray launch path. The presentation command has no bypass flag.

