{% if values.workspace.role == 'build' %}
Every GCC environment repeats the same compiler producer group. Every
environment builds its own Foundation and Core/build-tool roots with its own
compiler surface. Run `./cse-build login concretize`; it creates missing locks and
uses the approved Spack runtime to run `scripts/verify-lockfiles.py`. Do not
install if verification reports different GCC hashes or incorrect language
providers.

The environment is the build execution unit. `./cse-build compute install` is the
simple sequential convenience path; it is not a scheduler. Concurrent
installation is allowed only after the selected shared install tree passes the
filesystem prefix-lock smoke test and all eight locks pass verification. The
operator may then use the two wrapper surface commands on separate nodes, or
run distinct environments directly with bare Spack. The direct install command
is `spack -e <environment> install --only-concrete`. Exact shared hashes wait
on Spack's prefix/database locks and are reused after the first successful
install. Never launch the same environment twice, and give each direct Spack
process its own mutable `SPACK_USER_CACHE_PATH`. The prepared shell keeps
`SPACK_MISC_CACHE_PATH` in a builder-named partition below the shared
restricted misc-cache root. Before and after Spack, it restores and verifies
the restricted CSE-group contract across the workspace, source/misc caches,
views, modules, and file-backed build cache while keeping concurrent builders
out of the same mutable misc-index partition.
